@page "/render/auto"
@rendermode InteractiveAuto

<PageTitle>InteractiveAuto Render Mode</PageTitle>

<h1>InteractiveAuto Render Mode</h1>

<p>
    This page uses <code>@@rendermode InteractiveAuto</code>. The host chooses the best execution environment,
    either server interactive or WebAssembly interactive, based on runtime support.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Why this mode is chosen:</strong>
    Use <code>InteractiveAuto</code> when you want the framework to select the most appropriate interactive mode for the current host.
    It is the best default for components that require interactivity but should remain flexible across deployment models.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Best cases:</strong>
    page demos, mixed-host applications, and scenarios where you want a single component to work in both server and WASM hosts without changing markup.
</p>

